# shellcheck shell=bash
# Invocation behind output/evaluation/timestamp_report.csv,
# timestamp_summary.json and timestamp_skipped.csv (segment-boundary error
# of Whisper Large v3 on the first 500 rows of the AMI IHM test split).
#
# Job 8917980, 2026-09-27, at code 6f9bf56 with a clean tree, on an NVIDIA
# H100 80GB HBM3 (node htc-g059, account educ-lift), as its environment
# record and the summary's run and whisper blocks say. The record is in
# environment/au_ts_8917980.txt beside the original's results on ARC.
#
# The job reproduced the first committed run, job 7737896 (2026-05-28, a
# Tesla P100-PCIE-16GB on htc-g032, code not recorded), in every row and
# every column that run wrote. The card can still move a boundary. Job
# 7746137 (2026-05-31) ran the same decode on an H100 PCIe on htc-g055 and
# put the start of AMI_EN2002a_H03_MEE071_0068404_0068460 one 20 ms
# timestamp step later, at 0.22 s in place of 0.20 s, which raises
# MAE_start from 8.74 to 8.78 ms. Every other row matched in every column
# it wrote. It used the default report directory, so on ARC it wrote over
# job 7737896's files in ${DATA}/speech_transcription_env/output/evaluation/,
# which now hold its own.
#
# The script asks for any GPU. The h100 type on htc spans more than one
# card (the H100 PCIe of htc-g055 among them), and of its nodes only
# htc-g059 and htc-g060, whose cards are H100 80GB HBM3, have the nvlink
# feature, so the command below asks for the h100 type and that feature to
# repeat the run on its own card.
#
# MODEL, LIMIT and VAD_REFINE below are the script's defaults at 6f9bf56,
# written out so that a later change of a default cannot change what this
# record reproduces. REPORT_DIR is not: the default is the evaluation
# directory itself.
#
# Reproduce (from the repository root on ARC):
#   ( set -a; . hpc/runs/timestamps.env || exit 1; set +a
#     sbatch --account=educ-lift --gres=gpu:h100:1 --constraint=nvlink \
#       hpc/submit_benchmark_timestamps.sh )
#
# A reproduction writes to its own directory under repro/, so it cannot
# overwrite the ARC copy of the original run it is to be compared with.
# original: REPORT_DIR="${DATA}/speech_transcription_env/output/evaluation/audit2026/timestamps"
MODEL=openai/whisper-large-v3
LIMIT=500
VAD_REFINE=0
REPORT_DIR="${DATA}/speech_transcription_env/output/evaluation/repro/timestamps"
